<BlogPost
  title="Eclipse Now Offers Painted Finishes on ProCore Plywood"
  description="Painted Eclipse orders with a Maple or White interior now get painted ProCore plywood finished ends, wall tops, bottoms, and utility tops — the same upgrade stained orders received earlier in 2026. The 10% plywood upcharge is unchanged and applicable orders have already transitioned."
  author="Ben Miller"
  publishedDate="2026-09-15"
  ogImage="/images/blog/eclipse-painted-procore-plywood/procore-plywood-spec.webp"
>

<p>Good news for painted kitchens: <a href="/brands/eclipse-cabinetry/">Eclipse Full Access Cabinetry</a> now offers <strong>paint on ProCore plywood</strong>, joining the <a href="/playbook/eclipse-procore-veneer-finished-ends/">stained ProCore finishes introduced earlier this year</a>.</p>

<h2>What changed</h2>

<ul>
  <li>Painted finishes with a standard <strong>White or Maple interior</strong> now include <strong>painted ProCore plywood</strong> for <strong>finished ends, wall tops, bottoms, and utility tops</strong> — so painted jobs get the same upgraded construction as stained ones.</li>
  <li><strong>All applicable plywood orders have already transitioned</strong> to the new ProCore paint platform. No action is needed on existing orders.</li>
  <li>The <strong>plywood upcharge remains 10%</strong> — no pricing change.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The construction details</h2>

<div class="post-figure">
  <img src="/images/blog/eclipse-painted-procore-plywood/procore-plywood-spec.webp" alt="Eclipse plywood spec page: 10% upcharge; stained, painted, and laminate plywood construction notes" width="841" height="357" fetchpriority="high" />
</div>

<div class="spec-table-wrap">
  <table class="spec-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Finish type</th><th scope="col">Plywood construction</th><th scope="col">Interiors</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Stained</th><td>Sides, top, bottom, and adjustable shelves are 3/4″ plywood (plywood core with two MDF cross bands); top &amp; bottom in matching stain</td><td>Maple only</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Painted (new)</th><td>Sides, top, bottom, and adjustable shelves are 3/4″ plywood (plywood core with two MDF cross bands); top &amp; bottom in matching paint</td><td>Maple or White</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Laminates (Acrylic, HPL, PV, TFL)</th><td><strong>Partial Plywood</strong>: plywood case with integrated particleboard or MDF finished ends; wall top &amp; bottom panels stay plywood and match the interior finish</td><td>Per interior options chart</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Not available with the Linen Interior option</strong> on any plywood construction.</li>
  <li>As always, the <strong>interior finish must be compatible with the exterior finish</strong> (see the Interior Options chart in the spec book).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Why it matters</h2>

<p>Until now, a client who chose paint got a less complete plywood package than a client who chose stain. That gap is closed: the painted white kitchen — still the volume of the business — now gets plywood finished ends and tops at the same 10% upcharge.</p>

